.Sh NAME
.Nm mbt_peerdb_init ,
.Nm mbt_peerdb_insert ,
.Nm mbt_peerdb_find ,
.Nm mbt_peerdb_select ,
.Nm mbt_peerdb_count ,
.Nm mbt_peerdb_total ,
.Nm mbt_peerdb_free
.Nd Peer database management for BitTorrent.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In mbt/peerdb.h
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_peerdb_init "struct mbt_peerdb *db"
.Ft struct mbt_peer_entry *
.Fn mbt_peerdb_insert "struct mbt_peerdb *db" "const char *addr" "uint16_t port" "int source"
.Ft struct mbt_peer_entry *
.Fn mbt_peerdb_find "struct mbt_peerdb *db" "const char *addr" "uint16_t port"
.Ft struct mbt_peer_entry *
.Fn mbt_peerdb_select "struct mbt_peerdb *db"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_peerdb_count "struct mbt_peerdb *db" "enum mbt_peerdb_state state"
.Ft int
.Fn mbt_peerdb_total "struct mbt_peerdb *db"
.Ft void
.Fn mbt_peerdb_free "struct mbt_peerdb *db"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm mbt_peerdb
module provides a mechanism to manage and track the state of discovered peers in a Bit
torrent swarm. It maintains an internal database of peers, recording their
connection status (e.g., known, connecting, active, failed, or banned), the source
from which they were found (DHT, Tracker, PEX), and metadata such as the last time
they were seen.
.Sh FUNCTIONS
The following functions manage the peer database:
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_peerdb_init
Initializes an empty peer database structure.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_peerdb_insert
Inserts a new peer into the database or updates an existing one based on the
provided address and port. It also records the source of discovery. Returns a
pointer to the created or found
.Vt mbt_peer_entry.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_peerdb_find
Searches for a peer in the database using its IP address and port. Returns
.Fa NULL
if no matching peer is found.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_peerdb_select
Selects the best available peer to attempt a connection. This function
implements a selection strategy that prioritizes peers in the
.Vt MBT_PEERDB_KNOWN
state, preferring those with recent activity and fewer recorded failures. Returns
.Fa NULL
if no suitable peer is available.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_peerdb_count
Returns the number of peers currently in a specific
.Vt mbt_peerdb_state.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_peerdb_total
Returns the total number of peers present in the database.
.El
.Bl -tag -width 12
.It .Fn mbt_peerdb_free
Clears the database and frees all stored peer entries and resources.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mbt 3
